A||N||27||Jackalrr||How to pimp out the V6?||||5||
Z||000000||Jackalrr||11-15-2000||05:45 PM||||Hello,<P>I own an 85 Fiero GT. I would like to soup it up and get as much HP as possible. I am planning on the following upgrades:<P>Borla stainless steel exhaust<BR>Performance rebuild kit from <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A> <BR>Turbocharger<BR>and possibly new manifolds<P>Does anyone know of anything else that would increase horsepower or any other tricks for getting more power out of the 2.8 v6? I don't want to put a different engine in the car, I would prefer to keep the 6.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||11-15-2000||06:07 PM||||If you have the manual transmission an aluminum flywheel would make a very noticeable difference. You can get them from <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroshop.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||11-16-2000||12:41 AM||||Well, sounds like you've got a plan alright. The whole idea is to bring the most air/fuel in, blow it up good, and send it out as quick as is efficient.  I recommend a K&N filter, upgrade ignition system (I have Accel super coil, 8mm wires, and Bosch Platinums&gt; want to upgrade more with MSD 6A), and bolt that exhaust on quick. Other then that, there isn't to much more to do until you go forced induction- e.g. turbo, Nitrous Oxide.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||11-16-2000||02:01 AM||||pimp?||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||11-16-2000||07:51 AM||||If you want to "pimp-out" your motor, you're going to need lots of chrome and gold.  Also, get some of those tassle things that strippers attach to their nips.||||reg||14
